@startuml
title Run lifecycle (owned by ai-qa)

[*] --> CREATED : aiqa run
CREATED --> PREFLIGHT : run dir written
PREFLIGHT --> REFUSED : login required / env unknown, not READY, unhealthy / no scenarios / invalid scenario file
PREFLIGHT --> RUNNING : descriptor + scenarios loaded, session valid
RUNNING --> RUNNING : scenario finished (result recorded)
RUNNING --> COMPLETED : all scenarios have a result (or run budget exhausted -> rest SKIPPED)
RUNNING --> ABORTED : Ctrl-C / signal / unrecoverable runner error (children killed, partial results kept)
REFUSED --> [*]
COMPLETED --> [*]
ABORTED --> [*]

note right of RUNNING
  A run.json left in RUNNING whose pid is gone is shown as INTERRUPTED
  by `aiqa show`; it is never resumed (start a new run).
end note
@enduml

@startuml
title Scenario result (inside one run)

[*] --> PENDING
PENDING --> RUNNING : agent call started
RUNNING --> PASSED : VerdictGate accepts PASSED
RUNNING --> FAILED : agent says FAILED, or gate reason\n(timeout, turn_cap, agent_protocol, no_evidence, out_of_scope, agent_error)
RUNNING --> RUNNING : one retry on agent_protocol only
PENDING --> SKIPPED : run budget exhausted / filtered out
PASSED --> [*]
FAILED --> [*]
SKIPPED --> [*]
@enduml
